{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the actual plot price on Raebareli Road in 2026?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Plot prices vary significantly by zone and legal status. In Zone A (PGI Belt — Vrindavan Yojna area), approved resale plots range from ₹2,500–₹5,500/sqft depending on road width and location. In Zone B (DLF Corridor), DLF Garden City BSP is ₹2,100–₹2,500/sqft; Omaxe Metro City plots are ₹4,500–₹5,000/sqft. In Zone C (Mohanlalganj–Kisan Path), approved societies range ₹1,200–₹2,000/sqft; unapproved land drops to ₹700–₹1,200/sqft. The ₹6,000+ figures seen on portals are blended apartment averages — not plot rates."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Raebareli Road a good investment for plots in 2026?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes — specifically Zone B (DLF Corridor) for 3–5 year investors, and Zone A (PGI Belt) for rental income buyers. DLF entry plots at ₹2,100/sqft against Gomti Nagar Extension plots at ₹5,000–₹10,000/sqft represents a 50–75% entry discount on a corridor with confirmed infrastructure including SGPGI expansion, SCR Vigyan Path, and Kisan Path connectivity. The RRTS proposal adds further upside. However Zone C requires careful verification — significant unapproved inventory exists."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which is better — DLF Garden City or Omaxe Metro City for plots?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Different profiles suit different buyers. DLF Garden City has lower entry (₹2,100/sqft BSP vs ₹4,500/sqft for Omaxe plots) and larger plot sizes (2,700–4,500 sqft). Omaxe Metro City is closer to SGPGI (~1 km vs ~5 km for DLF) and offers smaller plot sizes from 1,200 sqft — better for buyers with ₹55–75L budgets. Both are LDA and RERA approved. For rental income, Omaxe wins on proximity to SGPGI. For long-term land appreciation, DLF wins on size and established township status."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I get a home loan for a plot on Raebareli Road?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, for LDA-approved and RERA-registered plots. DLF Garden City, Omaxe Metro City, Suraksha Enclave, Skyom City, and Vrindavan Yojna (UPAVP) all have bank loan approvals from major lenders including SBI, HDFC, ICICI, and Axis Bank. Unapproved Zila Panchayat plots and agricultural land are refused by all banks without exception — if a bank won't lend on it, you shouldn't buy it."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the minimum budget for a legal plot on Raebareli Road?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For a legally safe, RERA or LDA approved plot, the minimum realistic budget is ₹15–20 lakh for 1,000 sqft in Zone C approved societies or Vrindavan Yojna back-lane resale. For a gated township with full amenities (DLF, Suraksha, Omaxe), budget ₹47 lakh minimum. Below ₹15 lakh, almost all available plots are unapproved or agricultural — the legal risk at that price point is extremely high."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why are plot rates on portals showing ₹6,000/sqft for Raebareli Road?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Portal averages like ₹6,050/sqft (99acres) or ₹6,000/sqft are blended averages covering all property types — apartments, flats, independent houses, and plots combined. Apartment rates in gated societies skew these averages significantly upward. Actual plot-only transaction data shows rates of ₹900–₹5,500/sqft depending on zone and approval status. Always ask for plot-specific comparable transactions, not corridor averages."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are the risks of buying a plot near SGPGI on Raebareli Road?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The three main risks are: (1) Unapproved Zila Panchayat colonies sold as residential — no bank loan available, demolition risk from LDA; (2) Agricultural land sold as residential without mandatory land use conversion — cannot build, bank refuses financing; (3) The 'Registry ho gayi = safe' misconception — registration does not validate title, land use, or layout approval. Always verify RERA at up-rera.in, land use at upbhulekh.gov.in, and LDA layout at ldalucknow.in before paying anything."
      }
    }
  ]
}
